{"id":"torrey:manasseh-the-tribe-of","source":"torrey","name":"Manasseh, The Tribe Of","slug":"manasseh-the-tribe-of","seeAlso":[],"entries":[{"text":"Descended from Joseph’s eldest son adopted by Jacob — Ge 41:51; 48:5.","refs":[["Gen",41,51,41,51],["Gen",48,5,48,5]]},{"text":"Predictions respecting — Ge 48:20; 49:22-26; De 33:13-17.","refs":[["Gen",48,20,48,20],["Gen",49,22,49,26],["Deut",33,13,33,17]]},{"text":"To number the people. — Nu 1:10.","refs":[["Num",1,10,1,10]]},{"text":"To spy out the land. — Nu 13:11.","refs":[["Num",13,11,13,11]]},{"text":"To divide the land. — Nu 34:23.","refs":[["Num",34,23,34,23]]},{"text":"Strength of, on leaving Egypt — Nu 1:34,35.","refs":[["Num",1,34,1,34],["Num",1,35,1,35]]},{"text":"Part of third division of Israel in their journeys — Nu 10:22,23.","refs":[["Num",10,22,10,22],["Num",10,23,10,23]]},{"text":"Encamped next to, and under the standard of Ephraim west of tabernacle — Nu 2:18,20.","refs":[["Num",2,18,2,18],["Num",2,20,2,20]]},{"text":"Offering of, at dedication — Nu 7:54-59.","refs":[["Num",7,54,7,59]]},{"text":"Families of — Nu 26:29-33.","refs":[["Num",26,29,26,33]]},{"text":"Strength of, on entering Canaan — Nu 26:34.","refs":[["Num",26,34,26,34]]},{"text":"On Gerizim said amen to the blessing — De 27:12.","refs":[["Deut",27,12,27,12]]},{"text":"Half of, obtained inheritance east of Jordan — Nu 32:33,39-42; Jos 13:29-31.","refs":[["Num",32,33,32,33],["Num",32,39,32,42],["Josh",13,29,13,31]]},{"text":"Inheritance of the other half — Jos 17:1-11.","refs":[["Josh",17,1,17,11]]},{"text":"Could not drive out the Canaanites but made them tributary — Jos 17:12,13; Jdj 1:27,28.","refs":[["Josh",17,12,17,12],["Josh",17,13,17,13],["Judg",1,27,1,27],["Judg",1,28,1,28]]},{"text":"Aided David against Saul. — 1Ch 12:19-21.","refs":[["1Chr",12,19,12,21]]},{"text":"At coronation of David. — 1Ch 12:31-37.","refs":[["1Chr",12,31,12,37]]},{"text":"Returned to their allegiance to the house of David in Asa’s reign. — 2Ch 15:9.","refs":[["2Chr",15,9,15,9]]},{"text":"At Hezekiah’s passover. — 2Ch 30:1,11,18.","refs":[["2Chr",30,1,30,1],["2Chr",30,11,30,11],["2Chr",30,18,30,18]]},{"text":"David appointed rulers and captains over — 1Ch 26:32; 27:20,21.","refs":[["1Chr",26,32,26,32],["1Chr",27,20,27,20],["1Chr",27,21,27,21]]},{"text":"Often at war with Ephraim — Jdj 12:1,6; Isa 9:21.","refs":[["Judg",12,1,12,1],["Judg",12,6,12,6],["Isa",9,21,9,21]]},{"text":"Country of, purified from idols by Hezekiah and Josiah — 2Ch 31:1; 34:6.","refs":[["2Chr",31,1,31,1],["2Chr",34,6,34,6]]},{"text":"Daughters of Zelophehad. — Nu 27:1-7.","refs":[["Num",27,1,27,7]]},{"text":"Gideon. — Jdj 6:15.","refs":[["Judg",6,15,6,15]]},{"text":"Abimelech. — Jdj 9:1.","refs":[["Judg",9,1,9,1]]},{"text":"Jotham. — Jdj 9:5,7,21.","refs":[["Judg",9,5,9,5],["Judg",9,7,9,7],["Judg",9,21,9,21]]},{"text":"Jair. — Jdj 10:3.","refs":[["Judg",10,3,10,3]]},{"text":"Jephthah. — Jdj 11:1.","refs":[["Judg",11,1,11,1]]},{"text":"Barzillai. — 2Sa 17:27.","refs":[["2Sam",17,27,17,27]]},{"text":"Elijah. — 1Ki 17:1.","refs":[["1Kgs",17,1,17,1]]}],"refCount":50}
